     "p": "At a fixed threshold, TP denotes a correctly flagged positive, FP a falsely flagged negative, FN a missed positive, and TN a correctly unflagged negative. Accuracy is $(TP+TN)/(TP+FP+FN+TN)$, precision is $TP/(TP+FP)$, recall or sensitivity is $TP/(TP+FN)$, specificity is $TN/(TN+FP)$, and false-positive rate is $1-\\text{specificity}$. Each denominator must be checked: precision is undefined under the unmodified ratio if no case is flagged. State a reporting convention for that case."
