        "p": "**Bayes derivation.** Let $D$ mean a real leak and $S$ mean the alert exceeds a fixed threshold. Then $P(D\\mid S)=P(S\\mid D)P(D)/P(S)$. By total probability, $P(S)=P(S\\mid D)P(D)+P(S\\mid\\neg D)P(\\neg D)=r\\pi+f(1-\\pi)$. This yields the precision expression above. A case-control evaluation that deliberately samples equal numbers of leak and nonleak meters has $\\pi=.5$ by design, not necessarily by deployment. Estimate the deployment prior separately and verify that sensitivity and false-positive rate transport before using the formula. If sensor hardware changes, the score distribution conditional on each class may change, so only replacing $\\pi$ can be wrong. For a crew limit, precision at the top ten per day may be more informative than one threshold transported across days with different score distributions."
