     "p": "For binary decisions under a **specific simplified cost model**, suppose flagging a nonurgent ticket costs c_FP=1, missing an urgent ticket costs c_FN=10, and a correct action costs zero. If calibrated p is the probability of urgency and each action has the assumed effect, expected cost of flagging is (1-p)c_FP; expected cost of not flagging is p c_FN. Flag when"
